PE array area, T4_MAXDIM16_shipped_baseline
Source: the mapped database at /scratch/users/sk3463/build_T4_MAXDIM16_shipped_baseline/4-synopsys-dc-synthesis/
(no re-synthesis). DC W-2024.09, FreePDK45 view-standard, 3.33 ns, topographical,
flatten_effort 3, sram_mode='none'.

THERE IS NO PE-ARRAY HIERARCHY LINE. report_area -hierarchy carries accu_0_U0,
dma_ld_0_1_U0 and gmem0..3_m_axi_U, but no pe_R_C_U0 instance: at flatten_effort 3
DC dissolved every PE instance into the top level, so the array's area is inside
tinytpu_isa's local area. get_cells -hier confirms zero hierarchical pe_*_U0 cells.

The figures below are therefore a NAME-PREFIX SUM over flattened leaf cells, not a
hierarchy line: every non-hierarchical cell whose name begins pe_<row>_<col>_,
grouped by that prefix. 5,020 leaf cells matched, none unmatched.

  PE          area (um2)
  pe_0_0         870.352
  pe_0_1         653.296
  pe_0_2         653.296
  pe_0_3         617.120
  pe_1_0        1525.776
  pe_1_1        1308.720
  pe_1_2        1308.720
  pe_1_3        1236.368
  pe_2_0        1417.248
  pe_2_1        1308.720
  pe_2_2        1308.720
  pe_2_3        1236.368
  pe_3_0        1302.868
  pe_3_1        1736.980
  pe_3_2        2171.092
  pe_3_3        2532.852
  -----------------------
  total       21188.496   over 16 PEs
  mean          1324.28   um2/PE

Identical in both designs to the digit, which is expected: MAXDIM changes memory
depth, not the array.

Against Gemmini's published 116K um2 for 256 PEs = 453 um2/PE at 22 nm. A node
difference of 45/22 is about 4.2x in area, so that figure corresponds to roughly
1,900 um2/PE at 45 nm, against 1,324 um2/PE here. Treat as order-of-magnitude
only: the node scaling is a rule of thumb, the two PEs may not contain the same
functions (accumulator registers in particular), and the per-PE spread here
(617 to 2,533) shows DC optimising PEs differently by position, so a mean hides
structure. It is one clearly-named uncertainty rather than four compounding ones,
which was the point of asking.
